  "description": "Overview HackWithVizag-4.0 is a student hackathon designed to encourage innovation, problem-solving, and technology-driven solutions to real-world challenges by Nadimpalli Satyanarayana Raju Institute of Technology (NSRIT). The event consists of an Online Screening Round followed by an Offline Hackathon Round for shortlisted teams. Register Here: https://www.hackwithvizag.com Guidelines Open to college/university students. Team size: 3–4 members. Cross-college teams are not allowed. Participants can register in only one team. Multiple problem statements will be provided across different themes, along with an Open Innovation category. For the online round, teams must submit an abstract (150–200 words), PPT, supporting document (if applicable), and video link. Shortlisted teams will advance to the offline hackathon to develop and demonstrate their solution. Online participation is free. Offline participation fee: ₹500 per participant for shortlisted teams. Rules Teams must work on only one problem statement. Submissions must be original and developed by the participating team. Plagiarism, impersonation, cheating, or unfair practices will result in disqualification. Participants may use publicly available tools, frameworks, APIs, and datasets subject to their respective licenses. All submissions must be made within the specified deadlines. Judges' and organizers' decisions will be final and binding. Participants must follow the event guidelines and maintain professional conduct throughout the hackathon. Prizes 1st Prize: ₹40,000 2nd Prize: ₹20,000 3rd Prize: ₹10,000 Consolation Prize: ₹3,000 each Certificates will be awarded to all participants who complete the hackathon.",
