    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>HackWithVizag-4.0 is a student hackathon designed to encourage innovation, problem-solving, and technology-driven solutions to real-world challenges by Nadimpalli Satyanarayana Raju Institute of Technology (NSRIT). The event consists of an Online Screening Round followed by an Offline Hackathon Round for shortlisted teams.<br /><br />Register Here:<br />https://www.hackwithvizag.com</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to college/university students.</li>\n<li>Team size: 3&ndash;4 members.</li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are not allowed.</li>\n<li>Participants can register in only one team.</li>\n<li>Multiple problem statements will be provided across different themes, along with an Open Innovation category.</li>\n<li>For the online round, teams must submit an abstract (150&ndash;200 words), PPT, supporting document (if applicable), and video link.</li>\n<li>Shortlisted teams will advance to the offline hackathon to develop and demonstrate their solution.</li>\n<li>Online participation is free.</li>\n<li>Offline participation fee: ₹500 per participant for shortlisted teams.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must work on only one problem statement.</li>\n<li>Submissions must be original and developed by the participating team.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, impersonation, cheating, or unfair practices will result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Participants may use publicly available tools, frameworks, APIs, and datasets subject to their respective licenses.</li>\n<li>All submissions must be made within the specified deadlines.</li>\n<li>Judges' and organizers' decisions will be final and binding.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow the event guidelines and maintain professional conduct throughout the hackathon.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>1st Prize: ₹40,000</li>\n<li>2nd Prize: ₹20,000</li>\n<li>3rd Prize: ₹10,000</li>\n<li>Consolation Prize: ₹3,000 each</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Certificates will be awarded to all participants who complete the hackathon.</p>",
